    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16284" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕtēsĭae</span></b> ,
			ārum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐτησίαι</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμοι</span>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the winds that blow annually during the dog-days for
				forty days</i>, <i>Etesian winds</i>, <i>trade-winds</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Q. N. 5, 10 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 11,
				2, 56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">58</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Lucr.
				6, 716</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 53</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fam. 2,
				15 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; id. poët. Or. 45;
				<i><span class="en">Caes.
				B. C. 3, 107</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 37, 23</span></i> et saep.—In
				sing.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ete-sias</span></b> , ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἐτησίας</span>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 18,
				34, 77, § 335</span></i>.</div>
